Subject: Remove the hub self-update command

Origin: DHI-internal (packaged hub must not replace its own executable)
Description: Drop the always-registered update command and the file that downloads a release and replaces the running executable.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/henrygd/beszel.git e2ed147a5aa6472e6462521632ccc7101668132c
Verify: cmd `go test ./package/main/henrygd-beszel/tests -count=1 -run TestHubServes` expect "ok"
Forwarded: not-needed (a distro package must not download a release and overwrite its executable)
Drop-When: never: upstream registers this command on every hub build and the packaged binary must not replace itself

The hub command is registered unconditionally. Leaving it in the binary would let `beszel update` fetch a GitHub release and overwrite the installed executable. The HTTP update route stays in source and stays unregistered unless CHECK_UPDATES is set, which this package does not set.

diff --git a/internal/cmd/hub/hub.go b/internal/cmd/hub/hub.go
